    "result_text": "All 22 tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` on owner creation \u2014 the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same first name and last name, case-insensitively.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 before saving the new owner, count existing owners whose normalized first name and last name match the incoming owner's. Reused the existing `householdKey` helper (trim + collapse whitespace + lowercase) to get case-insensitive comparison, consistent with how the app already compares owner fields. The new owner isn't saved yet, so it's naturally excluded from the count.\n\n2. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added a persisted `namesakeCount` field (`namesake_count` column) with getter/setter, so it survives the create \u2192 GET read-back that the acceptance tests do.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `namesakeCount` (readOnly `int32`, min 0) to the `Owner` response schema, so the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` carries the field; MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column to each `owners` table (tests run on hsqldb; the others kept in sync).\n\nVerified: `Cp13Tests` passes, and the full suite is green (22/22).",
